# Data Universe — environment variables

This project is **fully static and local-first**: it runs with no environment
variables and no backend.

The file exists so future optional integrations (for example a self-hosted
proxy for an AI-assisted feature) have a documented place to declare keys.

Rules for any future variable added here:

1. Never commit real values. Only names and placeholder values belong in this file.
2. Anything used by the browser bundle is public by definition — do not put secrets in `VITE_*`.
3. Secrets must live in the platform's secrets store and be consumed server-side.

# --- Optional example (NOT used by the current build) ---
# Base URL of a user-configured OpenAI-compatible endpoint, proxied server-side.
# VITE_AI_BASE_URL=https://your-proxy.example.com/v1
